# Release recipe: build the module (test-gated), then publish the BUILT tree.
# Run with: box run-script release
#
# Requires the test server running on port 60310 (box run-script start:2023).
# The build aborts on any test failure, so a broken suite can never ship.
#
# ALWAYS release with `box run-script release`. Never run a bare `box publish`
# from the repo root: CommandBox reads .gitignore when it packages, so any
# unanchored ignore pattern silently strips matching source folders from the
# published module. That is how caffeinecms 1.0.0-beta.1 shipped with missing
# models and every app that installed it died at startup. buildSource() counts
# the zip contents and aborts on a mismatch, so this path is the guarded one.

# Fail fast if local main is not what the remote has.
!git checkout -f main
!git pull origin main

# Build: runs the FULL test suite first and aborts on any failure, then writes
# the slim module tree to .tmp/erroralerts/ and the distributable zip to
# .artifacts/erroralerts/<version>/.
run-script build:module

# Publish from the built tree, not the repo root, so ForgeBox receives exactly
# what the build produced (no reliance on box.json's ignore list).
cd .tmp/erroralerts
publish
cd ../../

# After a successful publish, tag the release by hand so the published
# artifact stays findable in git history:
#   git tag v<version> && git push origin main --tags
